+
+## Coupled-status operator reporting
+
+`src/coupled_status.rs` owns the read-only projection of native coupled-run records. It reads `iterations.json` and finalized or pending `.spiral-coder` work ledgers without changing persistence, invoking providers, or running tools. Request counts are derived only from durable ledger entries: `wire_requests` counts every request and `task_requests` counts `charge: task`, with omitted native charge treated as the task default. An absent interrupted ledger represents unknown usage with `null`; it is never converted to zero. The command's recorded completion status is an observation of the native manifest, not independent verification or promotion authorization. The projection is not persisted as a new state surface.
+
+## Coupled-status ownership
+
+`coupled-status` is a read-only projection owned by `src/coupled_status.rs`. It parses native iteration ledgers and does not add or persist a new state surface.
